	// HYPOTHESIS-2: A small BatchSize-specific penalty (separate from QueueDepth) will reduce cache_warmup_e2e_ms below 4205 by avoiding instances with large active batches that slow prefill
	// MECHANISM-2: During cache warmup, new requests need prefill compute; instances with large active batches have less compute available. BatchSize penalty steers prefill-heavy requests to instances with smaller active batches.
